# Routing Notes

- SAP work should be delegated to a specialized agent when available.
- If the target agent requires approval, ask the human supervisor first.
- Non-SAP work should remain with the main agent unless otherwise specified.

## SAP Helper Agent Handoff Notes

### When to Use sap-helper
- Any SAP system queries (read-only operations)
- SAP data extraction requests
- SAP report generation tasks
- SAP transaction assistance for standard operations

### When Escalation is Required (Human Approval from Ilkerkaan)
- SAP data modification operations
- SAP configuration changes
- SAP integration tasks
- Critical SAP system errors
- Data integrity issues
- Security-related SAP operations
- Tasks exceeding agent capability

### Auto-Approved Tasks
The following tasks can be executed by sap-helper without human approval:
- Read-only SAP queries
- Data extraction
- Report generation

### Approval Required Tasks
The following tasks require explicit approval from human supervisor (Ilkerkaan):
- SAP data modification
- SAP configuration changes
- SAP integration tasks

MARKER: ROUTING_NOTES_V2
EOF

